      "final_lf": false,
      "returned_content": "## CLI contract\n\n`--version` prints `newlangc 0.1.0 (P0 bootstrap)`. `--help` (also no arguments)\nprints usage; both exit 0. Invalid options / argument counts exit 2.\n\n`newlangc --check SOURCE` runs the same production parser, function-unit\nregistration and semantic checking of the ordinary `main()` entry, then\ndestroys the source-generated checked-owned fragment without invoking codegen.\nSuccess exits 0 with zero stdout/stderr bytes. Source I/O failures exit 1;\nparser and semantic failures retain their diagnostics and exit 3. A missing\nentry is a semantic failure. Backend-unsupported but semantically valid source\ncan pass `--check`; this does **not** establish C17, LLVM or native support.",
      "hash_scope": "returned range bytes only, not whole README"
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "inclusive_lines": "44-50",
      "git_blob_sha": "c0f2e0d7a91c55951a4fcc402acc7f42be70d12e",
      "returned_utf8_bytes": 417,
      "returned_text_sha256": "d797adb7d538476beb746715ee2cfc3d6d5197d5d5505acf46cfbff6de86c85c",
      "final_lf": false,
      "returned_content": "## Named C17 output (POSIX host)\n\nUse `newlangc --emit-c17-to OUTPUT.c SOURCE.nl` to preserve an existing output\nwhen compilation or saving fails. The compiler stages the same normal C17 bytes\nin a private sibling file, then replaces the target only after emission, flush\nand close succeed. Source aliases and symlink/special-file destinations are\nrefused. Default stdout and `--check` retain their existing behavior.",
      "hash_scope": "returned range bytes only, not whole README"
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "inclusive_lines": "404-411",
      "git_blob_sha": "c0f2e0d7a91c55951a4fcc402acc7f42be70d12e",
      "returned_utf8_bytes": 531,
      "returned_text_sha256": "8b7b752a21edc3ea84d16605d029227cb92a4b6188da772bbecbd998a3775b11",
      "final_lf": false,
      "returned_content": "For a source path, the bounded CLI path reads the actual source, parses the\nsource function unit, registers/checks it with the production semantic\nchecker, then checks an ordinary zero-argument `main()` call selected only\nby the driver. Only after these checks does `newlangc SOURCE` emit bounded\nC17 reference code to stdout, including the\n[initial Some fixture](#initial-some-first-user-quickstart-no-llvm).\nSemantic rejection emits no C bytes. Checked programs beyond the finite\nemitter profiles report `V1-BACKEND-UNSUPPORTED`.",
      "hash_scope": "returned range bytes only, not whole README"
    }
  ],
